              "task": "killing-all-sessions-wipes-restore-state-6-2",
              "source": "reviewer",
              "summary": "CLAUDE.md's state row still says the daemon's tick and shutdown flush pass its in-memory previous index.",
              "failure": "An agent working from CLAUDE.md would assume the daemon's merges and carry still read its lagging in-memory index, and might add another lag repair or hold extension this task made unnecessary, or write a test whose premise is false; nobody notices until the test unexpectedly passes or a reviewer catches it.",
              "detail": "CLAUDE.md state row: 'The daemon's tick and shutdown flush dump, passing the daemon's in-memory previous index.' and 'The caller's LoadPrev is called only once the lock is held.' Should say the cycle's previous index is sessions.json read under the lock, and LoadPrev (the daemon's in-memory index, or commit-now's re-read) supplies it only when that file cannot be read or decoded.",
              "files": [
                "CLAUDE.md"
              ]
            },
            {
              "task": "killing-all-sessions-wipes-restore-state-6-2",
              "source": "reviewer",
              "summary": "The commitNowFixture stand-in cycle still calls LoadPrev on every run.",
              "failure": "The fake no longer behaves like RunCommitCycle, which calls LoadPrev only when sessions.json cannot be read; a cmd test built on the fixture can assert behaviour that depends on LoadPrev and pass while the real command behaves differently. TestStateCommitNow_PassesPrevIndexFromDiskToCaptureAndRefile already pins the readable branch of commit-now's closure, which production no longer reaches.",
              "detail": "cmd/state_commit_now_test.go:90-96 is the fake (its comment says the previous index is loaded every cycle); :285-339 is the readable-path test. The `return idx` branch of loadPrevIndex (cmd/state_commit_now.go:172) can no longer run, because under the lock readPriorIndex and ReadIndex fail on exactly the same inputs. Fix: make the fake call LoadPrev only when the staged sessions.json does not decode, and fold the readable-path test into the real-cycle TestStateCommitNow_WarnsOnlyWhenSessionsJSONCannotBeRead.",
              "files": [
                "cmd/state_commit_now_test.go",
                "cmd/state_commit_now.go"
              ]
            },
            {
              "task": "killing-all-sessions-wipes-restore-state-6-2",
              "source": "reviewer",
              "summary": "Comments and docs around the daemon's LoadPrev still describe it as where the cycle's previous index comes from.",
              "failure": "Someone reasoning about which index the merges and the carry read (including an agent working from CLAUDE.md) gets the pre-fix answer, and might try to keep the daemon's in-memory index fresh or route a merge back through it, reopening the lag this task closed.",
              "detail": "cmd/state_daemon.go:423-424 says 'Skeleton-marked panes merge from this pre-boot state during the first capture' — false whenever a commit-now commits before that capture, and even on the normal path the merge reads sessions.json under the lock, not prevIdx. CLAUDE.md state row (line 61): 'The daemon's tick and shutdown flush dump, passing the daemon's in-memory previous index.' omits that the cycle merges from sessions.json and uses that index only as a fallback.",
              "files": [
                "cmd/state_daemon.go",
